    {
      "id": "review-acdb330950e3-1-review-1",
      "kind": "blocking",
      "status": "resolved",
      "acceptance_id": "ROG-S3-A1",
      "source": "review",
      "review_round": 2,
      "summary": "Fresh preparation discovers children through a Git-tracking precondition that its own commit is supposed to satisfy. At batch_preflight.ts:568–569, a batch containing only valid untracked child TaskIntents is rejected before any commit. With tracked and untracked children together, the workflow commit can make the latter enrollable while omitting their dirty source paths from the scope union, so the subsequent preflight rejects those in-scope paths as working_tree_dirty. Validate fresh child intents without requiring prior Git tracking before deriving the complete committable set, retain normal tracking and resume checks, and add all-untracked and mixed-child regression cases at the agreed Host seams.",
      "anchor": "sha256:466aa55ed2f52ef261a7f858901f8c7646a13638e1eaefe6c5a2b1abc6c14719",
      "evidence": {
        "trigger": "A non-resuming Initiative has valid, non-critical child intents with complete Spec bindings, but docs/plans/<child>.intent.json is untracked. Dirt consists only of workflow paths and source files inside those children's scopes. projectPreflight calls projectBatchPlan before commitWorkflowPaths. The unchanged batch_plan.ts:183 calls observeTaskIntent; the unchanged intent.ts:693–706 rejects an untracked sidecar. These unchanged paths were inspected because they directly implement child discovery used by the changed preparation entry. With no tracked children, preparation returns empty_enrollable_set without committing. With another tracked independent child, the commit tracks the new sidecar but leaves its source dirt behind because its scope was absent from recovery_children.",
        "caller_chain": [
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/claude/kernel_ports.ts:ClaudeRuntime.startPreparedBatch",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_preflight.ts:prepareBatchPreflight",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_preflight.ts:projectPlanSurface",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_plan.ts:projectBatchPlan",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/kernel/intent.ts:observeTaskIntent",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/kernel/intent.ts:readTaskIntentSource"
        ],
        "violated": {
          "kind": "acceptance",
          "ref": "ROG-S3-A1"
        }
      },
      "counterevidence": null
    },
    {
      "id": "review-acdb330950e3-2-review-2",
      "kind": "blocking",
      "status": "resolved",
      "acceptance_id": "ROG-S3-A2",
      "source": "review",
      "review_round": 2,
      "summary": "Automatic-commit failures reintroduce the manual commit demand for committable paths. batch_preflight.ts:608 maps a failed precondition commit to batch_run_rejected, whose recovery_action at batch_reasons.ts:174 says to 'commit working changes'. A failing pre-commit hook on docs/specs/draft.md therefore asks the user to perform the same in-scope commit this task removes. Give preparation failures a recovery action that reports the concrete Git error and directs repair and retry without requesting a manual commit; assert that recovery behavior in the existing dual-Host hook-refusal test.",
      "anchor": "sha256:af3d51ab6847950b76b818a38feddcbdeb6f4781b823470a91dc63ca612e9e13",
      "evidence": {
        "trigger": "A fresh batch has valid tracked child intents, an untracked docs/specs/draft.md, and a pre-commit hook that exits 1. commitWorkflowPaths throws, prepareBatchPreflight catches the error and resolves batch_run_rejected. Both Hosts return the recovery action 'delete or rename the conflicting branch, or commit working changes and retry in the current Host', despite the dirty path being inside the D12 committable set. tests/claude-batch-authority.test.ts:458–486 exercises this trigger on both Hosts but does not assert the recovery action.",
        "caller_chain": [
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/claude/kernel_ports.ts:ClaudeRuntime.startPreparedBatch",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_preflight.ts:prepareBatchPreflight",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/assurance/workflow_autocommit.ts:commitWorkflowPaths",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_preflight.ts:reject",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_reasons.ts:BATCH_REASONS.batch_run_rejected"
        ],
        "violated": {
          "kind": "acceptance",
